#concept-box("Adapt, then review")[
  The goal is meaningful and safe participation. A change that helps one participant may not help another, so ask, observe and adjust rather than relying only on a label.
]

== 8.4 Planning and Safety

Plan an activity around its purpose, the people involved, the environment, equipment and supervision. Inspect the area, explain the task clearly and agree on appropriate ways to communicate. Ensure that participants know how to report a problem and obtain assistance. For medical decisions or rehabilitation, seek appropriately qualified guidance rather than assuming that a general exercise is suitable for every person.

== 8.5 Four Worked Examples
#worked-example(1, "Leisure", tier: "FOUNDATION",
  [Time free from required work or obligations is commonly called \
A. leisure \
B. a ligament \
C. a fracture \
D. a sprint start],
  [Leisure generally refers to available free time. The answer is *A*.])
#worked-example(2, "A chosen activity", tier: "UTME STANDARD",
  [Reading for enjoyment during free time is an example of \
A. compulsory treatment \
B. recreation \
C. an artery \
D. a throwing sector],
  [Recreation can be a chosen quiet activity as well as a physical one. The answer is *B*.])
#worked-example(3, "An adaptation", tier: "UTME STANDARD",
  [A teacher changes the equipment after discussing a participant's needs. This is most directly \
A. automatic exclusion \
B. a medical diagnosis \
C. an activity adaptation \
D. a guarantee that no risk remains],
  [The equipment is adjusted to support participation; its suitability should be reviewed. The answer is *C*.])
#worked-example(4, "Individual needs", tier: "JAMB CHALLENGE",
  [Two participants share a diagnosis but have different preferences and abilities. The best general approach is to \
A. assume identical needs \
B. exclude both \
C. ignore their views \
D. discuss goals and select suitable individual adjustments],
  [A label alone does not determine individual needs; involve the people and review the adaptation. The answer is *D*.])

#trap-box("Avoid two false assumptions")[
  Recreation is not limited to competitive sport. A diagnosis or disability label does not tell you every activity a person can or cannot perform.
]

